WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.651
Almost everyone has heard of the Inuit people.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:09.310
We live in Canada, Russia, Greenland, and the state of Alaska.

3
00:00:09.311 --> 00:00:15.197
Many of my people are hunters, and we move around a lot.

4
00:00:15.198 --> 00:00:19.103
We hunt seals, walruses, and whales.

5
00:00:19.104 --> 00:00:22.244
But it is not easy to find these animals.

6
00:00:22.245 --> 00:00:25.316
Sometimes it takes many hours.

7
00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:30.674
Sometimes it takes many days.

8
00:00:30.675 --> 00:00:35.819
During winter, we need a warm place to sleep when we go hunting.

9
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.946
My ancestors invented the igloo.

10
00:00:38.947 --> 00:00:41.115
Igloo means house.

11
00:00:41.116 --> 00:00:43.410
It is a house made of snow.

12
00:00:43.411 --> 00:00:48.506
My father and I will show you how to build an igloo.

13
00:00:48.507 --> 00:00:51.722
First, you need to make snow blocks.

14
00:00:51.723 --> 00:00:56.526
The snow must be hard or it will be difficult to make an igloo.

15
00:00:56.527 --> 00:01:01.103
Cut bigger and heavier blocks for the bottom.

16
00:01:01.104 --> 00:01:04.082
Shape the snow blocks with a spade.

17
00:01:04.083 --> 00:01:07.513
The tops of the blocks are cut on an angle.

18
00:01:07.514 --> 00:01:13.470
This way, they form a dome when you put them on top of each other.

19
00:01:13.471 --> 00:01:16.091
Arrange the blocks in a circle.

20
00:01:16.092 --> 00:01:20.920
Use two blocks to make the door, and another for its roof.

21
00:01:20.921 --> 00:01:23.957
Dig out the snow on the igloo's floor.

22
00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:30.897
Now there will be more room inside the igloo, and it will be warmer too.

23
00:01:30.898 --> 00:01:33.983
For the top, use smaller blocks.

24
00:01:33.984 --> 00:01:36.884
Keep throwing snow out as you go.

25
00:01:36.885 --> 00:01:43.329
Now the igloo looks like a small dome.

26
00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.555
Go inside the igloo.

27
00:01:45.556 --> 00:01:48.581
Place the last few blocks from inside.

28
00:01:48.582 --> 00:01:52.092
Next, fill in all the cracks with snow.

29
00:01:52.093 --> 00:01:57.887
Then, use your hand to smooth the igloo walls.

30
00:01:57.888 --> 00:02:01.479
The igloo's door should be on an angle too.

31
00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:06.456
It should be dug deep to keep the cold air from blowing into the igloo.

32
00:02:06.457 --> 00:02:10.352
This also stops unwanted visitors like bears.

33
00:02:10.353 --> 00:02:14.685
Now our igloo is finished!

34
00:02:14.686 --> 00:02:18.932
My father makes a hole in the roof so we can cook.

35
00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:22.585
Don't worry! The fire will not melt our igloo.

36
00:02:22.586 --> 00:02:29.266
As the hot air from the fire rises, the cold air outside immediately freezes it.

37
00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:33.251
The snow blocks become harder.

38
00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:36.874
We use whale fat to make a small fire.

39
00:02:36.875 --> 00:02:38.885
Fish is my favorite.

40
00:02:38.886 --> 00:02:41.612
We sit on animal skins to eat.

41
00:02:41.613 --> 00:02:46.910
It is very warm and cozy inside our igloo.

42
00:02:46.911 --> 00:02:51.568
After a good night's sleep, we are ready to hunt again.

43
00:02:51.569 --> 00:02:56.257
For the Inuit, making an igloo takes only a short time.

44
00:02:56.258 --> 00:03:02.839
With an igloo, we can survive the cold winters.

45
00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:09.162
My ancestors invented a clever and unique shelter to stay in when we are hunting.

46
00:03:09.163 --> 00:03:23.577
How proud I am to be an Inuit and to sleep in an igloo, the amazing snow house!

